  "recommendation": "Show the trial grid itself as the primary UI representation. Do not score. Render each verified record as a literal visual reproduction of the experimental design: the tested treatment levels as discrete labelled points on a strip, the best-tested point highlighted, and the live sensor reading positioned on that same strip. The user sees WHERE they are relative to what was tested, not a fabricated continuous judgement. Call this a 'trial-position indicator'.",
  "why": [
    "A score curve requires interpolation between grid points. The data explicitly forbids treating best-tested-points as optima, so any interpolation fabricates meaning the evidence does not contain. Showing the grid itself is the only representation that adds zero invented information.",
