  "sketch": "## Schema additions\n\nTable `trial_position_indicator` in SQLite:\n```\nCREATE TABLE trial_position_indicator (\n  record_id         TEXT PRIMARY KEY,  -- FK to evidence record id\n  crop              TEXT,              -- NULL for common axes\n  axis              TEXT NOT NULL,\n  claim_role        TEXT NOT NULL,\n  grid_points_json  TEXT NOT NULL,     -- JSON array of tested levels, e.g. [11,17,23,29,35]\n  best_tested_value REAL,             -- the winning grid point, NULL if no single best\n  best_tested_unit  TEXT NOT NULL,\n  grid_bounded_above BOOLEAN NOT NULL, -- false if best == max(grid_points)\n  grid_bounded_below BOOLEAN NOT NULL, -- false if best == min(grid_points)\n  prohibited_use    TEXT NOT NULL,\n  cultivar          TEXT,\n  growth_stage      TEXT,\n  photoperiod_hours REAL,\n  measurement_basis TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n```\n\nExact rows from verified evidence:\n- basil temp: grid=[11,17,23,29,35], best=29, bounded_above=TRUE (35 tested, declined), bounded_below=TRUE\n- basil light: grid=[300,400,500,600], best=500 (author target, not strictly best—600 equalled it), bounded_above=TRUE, bounded_below=TRUE\n- peppermint light: grid=[20,100,150,200,250], best=NULL (band 150-200), bounded_above=TRUE (250 showed photoinhibition), bounded_below=TRUE\n- wasabi temp: grid=[10,14,18,22,26] (from 10/10 to 26/26 sweep), best=18, bounded_above=TRUE, bounded_below=TRUE\n- wasabi light: grid=[35,60,90,140], best=140, bounded_above=FALSE, bounded_below=TRUE\n- lettuce temp: grid=[15/10,23/18,30/23] (as ordinals 0,1,2 with labels), best=23/18, bounded_above=TRUE, bounded_below=TRUE\n- lettuce light: grid=[8.64,11.5,14.4] (DLI), best=11.5, bounded_above=TRUE (14.4 declined), bounded_below=TRUE\n- coriander light: grid=[133,200,400] x photoperiod [8,16,24] (2D factorial), best=(200,16), bounded_above=TRUE for PPFD (400 tested), bounded_below=TRUE\n\n## UI rendering (per axis card)\n\nFor a crop with evidence:\n```\n[Basil · Air Temperature · Vegetative (Nufar, 3 wk)]\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n 11°C    17°C    23°C   ⬤29°C    35°C↓\n  ○───────○───────○──────●────────○\n                              ▲ 27.3°C (now)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n● = best tested  ○ = tested  ↓ = declined at this level\n▲ = current sensor reading\nSource: Walters & Currey 2019, Nufar, growth chambers\n\"This is where your reading falls among the levels\n actually tested. It is NOT a score.\"\n```\n\nFor unbounded-above (wasabi light):\n```\n[Wasabi · Plant Light · Daruma, 12h photoperiod]\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n 35      60      90     ⬤140    ???\n  ○───────○───────○──────●─ ─ ─ ▸\n                         ▲ 128 PPFD (now)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n● = best tested (highest tested, optimum unknown above)\n▸ = untested region (no evidence of harm OR benefit)\n```\n\nFor empty crops:\n```\n[Cherry Tomato · Air Temperature]\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n  No comparative trial meets verification criteria.\n  Current reading: 24.1°C\n  See: supplementary research priorities\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n```\n\nFor disease risk (basil RH — NOT a grid, uses threshold indicators):\n```\n[Basil · Relative Humidity · Downy Mildew Risk]\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Infection risk:  canopy RH ≥ 85%    NOW: 72% ✓\n  Sporulation:     night RH > 95%\n                   sustained > 7.5 h  NOW: not night\n  Leaf wetness:    ≥ 4 h              NOW: no sensor\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n⚠ These are disease conditions, NOT growth optima.\n```\n\nFor PM (multi-time-base, no grid — reference bands):\n```\n[Common · PM2.5 · Human Health]\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n  WHO 24h guideline:    15 µg/m³\n  KR forecast bands:    Good ≤15 | Moderate ≤35 | Bad ≤75 | Very Bad >75\n  KR alert trigger:     Advisory 75 (2h sustained) | Warning 150 (2h sustained)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Sensor 24h rolling:   11.2 µg/m³  [within WHO 24h]\n  Sensor 2h rolling:    14.8 µg/m³  [below KR advisory]\n  ⚠ Low-cost sensor. Not equivalent to regulatory measurement.\n```\n\n## What 'distance-to-anchor' means in this design\n\nThe live reading's signed distance to the best-tested-point is the ONLY derived number: `delta = reading - best_tested_value`. This is displayed as a physical position on the strip. It is NOT a score because:\n- It has the original physical unit (°C, µmol/m²/s)\n- It does not claim the best-tested-point is optimal\n- It does not claim the delta maps to any growth outcome\n- It does not interpolate between grid points\n\n## Procurement signal\n\nThis design emits a clear procurement signal: the UI physically cannot render a plant_light strip unless the sensor outputs PPFD. A lux sensor produces a reading that cannot be placed on any tested-level strip because the strips are denominated in µmol/m²/s. The UI would show 'unit mismatch — cannot position reading on trial grid'. This makes the PPFD sensor requirement self-enforcing through the representation layer.",
